IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `on-ow`
IMPORT `on-ow-dates`
IMPORT `on-ow-seat`

-- Ontario Works -- worked cases from the seat of the applicant or recipient. Every assertion is a claim about the
-- ENCODING on stated facts. Expected values were worked by hand from the deposited text (the Act and O. Reg. 134/98),
-- never copied from the encoding's output. All the people are HYPOTHETICAL.
-- © King's Printer for Ontario, 1997 and 1998. NOT AN OFFICIAL VERSION.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 11 (1), (3): applying on one's own behalf.
#ASSERT `Can I apply on my own behalf` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (`Can I apply on my own behalf` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`Can I apply on my own behalf` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 38 (1): the asset limit.
#ASSERT `What is my asset limit` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` 10000
#ASSERT `What is my asset limit` TRUE 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` 15000
-- A couple with two children: $15,500 for the couple and one child, $500 for the second: $16,000.
#ASSERT `What is my asset limit` TRUE 0 2 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` 16000
-- A couple with an adult dependant and a child: the same, $16,000.
#ASSERT `What is my asset limit` TRUE 1 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` 16000
-- A sole support parent with one child: $10,500; with three: $11,500.
#ASSERT `What is my asset limit` FALSE 0 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` 10500
#ASSERT `What is my asset limit` FALSE 0 3 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` 11500
-- Not covered: an ODSP applicant (s 38 (2)); an application on behalf of a child only (s 38 (1) (e)).
#ASSERT `What is my asset limit` FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `an applicant for ODSP takes the ODSP asset limit (s 38 (2)), which is not encoded`
#ASSERT `What is my asset limit` FALSE 0 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `assistance on behalf of a dependent child only (s 11 (2), (4); s 38 (1) (e)) is not encoded`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 41 (1), s 42: budgetary requirements.
-- Single, rent $1,200 with heat included: $343 + the lesser of $1,200 and $390 = $733.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1200 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 733
-- Single, shelter $300: $343 + $300 = $643.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 300 100 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 643
-- Single, shelter $450 of which heat $420: heat exceeds the $390 maximum, so shelter is $420 (s 42 (2) para 4): $763.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 450 420 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 763
-- Sole support parent, one child, rent $1,100: $360 + $642 (unit of 2) = $1,002.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1100 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1002
-- Couple, two children, rent $1,500: $494 + $756 (unit of 4) = $1,250.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` TRUE 0 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1500 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1250
-- Couple, one adult dependant and one child, rent $800: $652 + $756 = $1,408.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` TRUE 1 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 800 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1408
-- No spouse, two adult dependants, rent $500: $781 + $500 (under the $697 maximum for 3) = $1,281.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 2 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 500 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1281
-- No spouse, four adult dependants, rent $2,000: $956 + $175 = $1,131; shelter $815 (unit of 5): $1,946.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 4 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2000 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1946
-- No spouse, two adult dependants and two children, rent $900: basic needs $781 (finding 3), shelter $815: $1,596.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 2 2 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 900 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1596
-- North of the 50th parallel without road access: single, rent $400: $343 + $390 + $272 = $1,005.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 400 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1005
-- North, couple and one child, rent $700: $494 + $502 + $697 = $1,693.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` TRUE 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 700 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1693
-- North, sole parent with three children, rent $900: $360 + ($526 + $102) + $756 = $1,744.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 900 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1744
-- Special diet determined at $300: capped at $250: $343 + $390 + $250 = $983.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 390 0 300 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 983
-- Couple, special diets $50 and $100, rent $700: $494 + $642 + $150 = $1,286.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` TRUE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 700 0 50 100 0 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 1286
-- Single aged 65: + $44: $777.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 390 0 0 0 1 0 0 EQUALS `answered` 777
-- Pregnant, non-dairy diet confirmed: + $50: $783; otherwise + $40: $773.
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 390 0 0 0 0 1 0 EQUALS `answered` 783
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 390 0 0 0 0 0 1 EQUALS `answered` 773
-- Not covered: board and lodging (ss 43, 44); shared custody (s 44.2); a sponsored immigrant with the sponsor (s 51).
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 390 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `not covered` `board and lodging, a long-term care home, a hostel or a community residence (O. Reg. 134/98 ss 43, 44) is not encoded`
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 1 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 900 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `not covered` `a child in shared custody halves the child's amounts (s 44.2), which is not encoded`
#ASSERT `What are my budgetary requirements` FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 390 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS `not covered` `a sponsored immigrant living with the sponsor (s 51) is not encoded`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 48, 49: income.
-- A recipient earning $1,000 gross, $100 deducted: $900 - $200 = $700; half of it, $350, counts.
#ASSERT `How much of my income counts` 1000 100 1 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 350
-- The same person applying (or in the first three months): the $200 and 50% are not applied: $900 counts (para 3).
#ASSERT `How much of my income counts` 1000 100 1 0 0 0 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 900
-- Applying, but back within six months after three months on assistance with earnings: $350 (para 4).
#ASSERT `How much of my income counts` 1000 100 1 0 0 0 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 350
-- Two adults earning $2,000 in all, $300 deducted: $1,700 - $400 = $1,300; $650 counts.
#ASSERT `How much of my income counts` 2000 300 2 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 650
-- $2,000 gross, licensed child care $200 and $800 of other child care for one child (capped at $600): $1,800 / 2 = $900,
-- less $800 = $100; plus $500 of EI: $600.
#ASSERT `How much of my income counts` 2000 0 1 200 800 1 500 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 600
-- $150 of earnings: under the $200 exemption, nil.
#ASSERT `How much of my income counts` 150 0 1 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- $800 of EI only: counts in full (s 49 (2), (3): not earnings).
#ASSERT `How much of my income counts` 0 0 0 0 0 0 800 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 800

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Act s 7 (3) and s 40 (1): eligibility and amount.
-- Single, requirements $733, income $350, assets $5,000 under $10,000: eligible; $383 a month.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for Ontario Works` TRUE TRUE 733 350 5000 10000 TRUE
#ASSERT `How much Ontario Works a month` 733 350 EQUALS 383
-- Income $800 exceeds requirements $733: not eligible; nil.
#ASSERT (`Am I eligible for Ontario Works` TRUE TRUE 733 800 5000 10000 TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `How much Ontario Works a month` 733 800 EQUALS 0
-- Assets exactly $10,000 "do not exceed" the limit: eligible; $10,001: not.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for Ontario Works` TRUE TRUE 733 0 10000 10000 TRUE
#ASSERT (`Am I eligible for Ontario Works` TRUE TRUE 733 0 10001 10000 TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Not resident in Ontario; not giving the information; not able to apply on own behalf: not eligible.
#ASSERT (`Am I eligible for Ontario Works` FALSE TRUE 733 0 0 10000 TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`Am I eligible for Ontario Works` TRUE TRUE 733 0 0 10000 FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`Am I eligible for Ontario Works` TRUE FALSE 733 0 0 10000 TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- A single applicant with no income and rent over $390: the full $733.
#ASSERT `How much Ontario Works a month` 733 0 EQUALS 733

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ss 69, 72: dates.
#ASSERT `By when must I request an internal review` (Date 1 10 2026) EQUALS Date 31 10 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I appeal` (Date 20 11 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) EQUALS Date 20 12 2026
-- A decision final late: the one-year limit from the original decision (1 October 2027) comes first.
#ASSERT `By when must I appeal` (Date 25 9 2027) (Date 1 10 2026) EQUALS Date 1 10 2027

-- The review and appeal path: request on day 10, review completed on day 35 (25 days later), appeal filed on day 50.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the internal review and appeal` 0 (LIST EVENT `the applicant or recipient` `request an internal review in writing` 10, EVENT `the administrator` `complete the internal review and give the decision` 35, EVENT `the applicant or recipient` `file a notice of appeal with the Social Benefits Tribunal` 50) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY `the administrator`, "internal review not completed within 30 days of the request (O. Reg. 134/98 s 70 (1))" -- the review is requested on day 10 and completed on day 45.
#TRACE `the internal review and appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant or recipient` DOES `request an internal review in writing` AT 10
    PARTY `the administrator` DOES `complete the internal review and give the decision` AT 45
-- expect: FULFILLED -- no review is requested; the 30 days pass (an unrelated event on day 40 moves time on).
#TRACE `the internal review and appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the administrator` DOES `complete the internal review and give the decision` AT 40
